# What the pins in sources.lock are for: build/pins-table.sh joins this file
# with sources.lock into the overview tables of the README and the release
# notes. Versions and commits come from sources.lock only, never from here.
#
#   product <id> | <name> | <sources> | <how it is tested>
#   change  <source> | <base> | <what it changes or fixes> | <how the change is tested> | <upstream>
#
# A "change" line is for every pin that is not a plain upstream release: a
# fork commit or a development commit. Fields are Markdown, one line each.
# <upstream>: the pull requests and issues (owner/repo#N, space-separated)
# that carry the change upstream; check-upstream.sh reports their state, and
# once all are merged or fixed the pin can go back to an upstream release.

product linux        | Linux client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_linux_x86_64 python_linux_aarch64 | `build/check-portable.sh` (only glibc ≥ 2.34, libgcc_s and libpulse from the host), `test/smoke.sh` (starts and finds its libraries on Alma 9, Rocky 10, Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Fedora 43, Tumbleweed, Arch; there the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk)
product windows      | Windows client `sdl-freerdp.exe` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d zlib jansson llvm_mingw freerdp_tk python_windows_x86_64 python_windows_aarch64 | `build/check-windows.sh` (needs only Windows' own DLLs)
product macos        | macOS client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_macos_arm64 python_macos_x86_64 | `build/check-macos.sh` (only macOS's own libraries and frameworks, minimum macOS 12.0, an ad-hoc signature); the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk; arm64 on macos-15, x86_64 on macos-15-intel
product web          | Web client + freerdp-web page | freerdp sdl3_wasm sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_web | `test/wasm-session.sh`: a browser logs in to xrdp through SSH + websockify, the page served without COOP/COEP headers (as GitHub Pages)
product xrdp         | xrdp packages (.deb, .rpm) | xrdp xorgxrdp x264 opus pipewire_xrdp | `check-deps.sh`, then `test/xrdp-session.sh`: install in a fresh container of each release, log in over RDP, an Xorg session with an xterm comes up
product xrdp-preview | xrdp preview packages | xrdp_preview librfxcodec libpainter xorgxrdp_preview x264 opus | `test/xrdp-session.sh --preview`: the Xorg login, then a Wayland one (sway) captured at the client's size

change freerdp          | FreeRDP master @ b2403bb99 (2026-10-23) | our release, picked from integration-latest on the fork; every client, native and web, builds it, not an upstream release; master has the Opus microphone fix #13810 that 3.32.2 lacks, and our merged AV1 #13731, sound #13732, H.264 through WebCodecs #13812, #13838, #13839. 5 commits of open pull requests for Emscripten builds (not compiled natively): clipboard #13733, microphone #13811, each as of 2026-10-25, the MessageChannel yield #13864 (pollset_poll's yield waits on a MessageChannel task, not setTimeout's clamped 4 ms; as of 2026-10-26), the page's monitors #13865 (the page splits the one canvas into a monitor per screen for the display layout; as of 2026-10-26), and no connection dialog window #13860 (its SDL window took the session's canvas: after a reconnect the canvas was 0 x 0 and the keys went nowhere; as of 2026-10-25). 1 commit of an open pull request for every client: SDL3 clipboard events with every field set #13872 (a pushed clipboard event left num_mime_types to the stack, and a negative value aborted the client on the server's next copy; as of 2026-10-26) | the native clients' smoke and xrdp login tests, the web login test; freerdp-web's suite on Asyncify and JSPI (22 of 22) and a forced-yield throughput check (53–57 → 1913–2291 kB/s); each pull request's own CI upstream | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13733 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13811 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13864 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13865 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13860 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13872
change sdl3_wasm        | SDL `release-3.4.18` | 1 commit: the Emscripten timers are safe to use from any thread. Since 4d8f84f161 (in 3.2.30 and 3.4) they run with pthreads too, but a timeout belongs to the thread that set it: a timer removed from another thread fired through a freed entry ("table index is out of bounds" in `SDL_Emscripten_TimerHelper`), in about 1 of 3 first sessions. 3.4.18 already has upstream's `FS.mkdir("/tmp/filedrop")` guard, which 3.2.30 needed backported (a second window, FreeRDP's retry dialog, threw `EEXIST` and hung a JSPI client after a network drop) | freerdp-web's whole suite on Asyncify and JSPI builds, 28 of 28 runs, `test-capture` and `test-reconnect` included, with the page's pointer-event fix (SDL 3.4 reads the mouse from pointer events); `SDL_timer.c` compiles with `-Werror` | libsdl-org/SDL#16587
change freerdp_tk       | its release {version} | our own connection window (Tkinter), shipped with the clients and their Python; `freerdp-tk` / `freerdp-tk.cmd` starts it | the smoke test loads it with the bundled Python on every distribution
change freerdp_web      | its release {version} | our own page, taken by its release tag | its unit tests and page checks (freerdp-web CI), then the web login test
change xrdp_preview     | xrdp devel @ 5943357a (2026-10-14) | 127 commits on their way upstream: Wayland sessions (wlup: sway, GNOME, KDE), GNOME and KDE with a monitor per RDP monitor and the client's primary as their own (branches feature-wlup-mutter-multimon, feature-wlup-kwin-multimon), and a max_fps setting for them, KWin 6.8's custom modes (kde_output_management_v2 22), AV1 with 4:4:4, encoder paced by the client's frame acknowledgements, Opus sound fixes (#3922: 2 of its 3 commits); plus the JPEG quality byte compared as unsigned, so it builds on ARM64 (branch caps-jpeg-quality-unsigned) | the preview login test, Xorg and Wayland, on x86_64 and ARM64; the ARM64 fix also by a build with -funsigned-char, which fails without it | neutrinolabs/xrdp#3904 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3911 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3912 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3913 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3914 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3915 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3922
change librfxcodec      | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp_preview` uses | built with the xrdp preview
change libpainter       | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp_preview` uses | built with the xrdp preview
change xorgxrdp_preview | xorgxrdp devel | unchanged: the development commit whose module interface `xrdp_preview` needs | the preview's Xorg login
change x264             | x264 `stable` branch | unchanged: x264 has no releases | the xrdp login tests (H.264)
change pipewire_xrdp    | release v{version} | unchanged, pinned by its tag's commit; built for Fedora only, which does not package it | built in the Fedora xrdp jobs
